You're working on the ESI.ts project at D:\code\ESI.ts, a TypeScript wrapper for the EVE Online ESI API. We're adopting Zod for runtime response validation.

Your task: Create `src/schemas/common.ts` with foundational Zod schemas.

The existing types in `src/types/common.ts` are:

```ts
export interface RateLimitMeta {
  remaining: number;
  limit: number;
  used: number;
  group: string | null;
}

export interface EsiResponseMeta {
  headers: Record<string, string>;
  fromCache: boolean;
  stale: boolean;
  cacheHitType?: 'spec-ttl' | 'etag-304' | 'stale-on-error';
  warning?: { code: number; message: string };
  requestId?: string;
  date?: string;
  contentLanguage?: string;
  rateLimit?: RateLimitMeta;
  responseTimeMs?: number;
}

export interface EsiResponse<T> {
  data: T;
  meta: EsiResponseMeta;
}
```

Create `src/schemas/common.ts` that:
1. First create the directory `src/schemas/` if it doesn't exist (run `ls src/` first to check)
2. Imports `z` from 'zod'
3. Defines `RateLimitMetaSchema` matching the RateLimitMeta interface exactly (group is `z.string().nullable()`)
4. Defines `EsiResponseMetaSchema` matching EsiResponseMeta exactly, using `.passthrough()` so extra fields don't cause validation errors
5. Defines a generic `esiResponse<T extends z.ZodTypeAny>(dataSchema: T)` function that returns `z.object({ data: dataSchema, meta: EsiResponseMetaSchema })`
6. Exports all schemas and the helper function

Also create `src/schemas/index.ts` as a barrel file that re-exports everything from `./common`.

Do NOT modify `src/types/common.ts` — another agent is handling that.
